# Customize guardrails (__BUNDLE__)

This plugin is the chock bundle `__BUNDLE__`. Each member below can be switched on or off; an absent
entry is on. The file that switches them is `.chock/guardrails.json` in a repository (committed, so a
pull request that turns one off is reviewed as a loosening) or `~/.chock/guardrails.json` outside one.
A repository's own file governs it; the user file counts only where the repository has none.

## Members

| Policy | What it does in this agent |
|---|---|
__MEMBERS__

The self-protection that refuses an agent's write to the toggle file is built in and is not a member:
it cannot be switched off.

## Procedure

1. Show the current state: run `chock bundle status` (it only reads), or read the governing file; a
   file that is invalid, or that differs from what `chock bundle` last recorded, switches nothing off,
   so every member is on. Show every member with its state
   and the label above.
2. When the person picks a member to switch, print the exact command for them to run in their own
   shell, one per member:
   - `chock bundle off <policy-id> --bundle __BUNDLE__` (add `--scope user` outside a repository);
   - `chock bundle on <policy-id> --bundle __BUNDLE__` to switch it back.
   In a repository that carries its own file, give no `--scope user` command: say the repository
   governs itself and give the repo-scope command for a pull request instead.
3. Stop there. The person runs the command.
4. If a turn end is refused because a toggle file "was changed outside `chock bundle`", say so and give
   the person both ways out: re-apply the intended state with `chock bundle on|off`, or review the file
   and run `chock bundle status --adopt`. Do not repair or adopt it yourself.

## Never

- Never write, edit, move, copy, link or delete `.chock/guardrails.json` or `~/.chock/guardrails.json`,
  or its record under `.chock/state/`, and never run `chock bundle on`, `chock bundle off` or
  `chock bundle status --adopt` yourself, even when asked: the built-in guard
  refuses it, and a guardrail switched off by the agent it constrains is no guardrail. Offer the
  command instead.
- Never put a pattern, path or rule in the file: it holds `on` or `off` per policy and nothing else.
- Never decide on the person's behalf which member to switch off; show the rows and let them choose.
